What is Maven :-
Maven is a build automation and dependency management tool for Java projects.
Maven takes your Java source code and turns it into a runnable application,
while also managing the libraries your application needs.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Where does Maven get its instructions?
The maven gets instruction form pom.xml
POM = Project Object Model

pom.xml
   ↓
Instructions for Maven
   ↓
Maven builds the application
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
What happens when you run Maven?
mvn clean package
Source Code
    ↓
Compile
    ↓
Test
    ↓
Package
    ↓
JAR file

src/main/java/
        ↓
      Maven
        ↓
target/
        ↓
spring-boot-web.jar
That JAR is the actual packaged Java application.
